Question 3 (Beginner → Intermediate: Arrays and Loops)
Problem:
Write a Java program that:

Asks the user how many numbers they want to enter.

Takes that many integers as input and stores them in an array.

Calculates and displays:

The largest number

The smallest number

The sum of all numbers

The average (as a double)

Hints/Requirements:

Use a for loop to fill the array.

Use another for loop to process (find max, min, sum).

Average = sum ÷ total count (cast to double).

This problem will help you practice:

Arrays

Loops

Basic math



import java.util.Scanner;

public class practice {
   public practice() {
   }

   public static void main(String[] var0) {
    Scanner sc= new Scanner(System.in);

    System.out.println("How many numbers will you input ?");
    int n = sc.nextInt();

    int [] array = new int[n];
    for(int i =0; i<n; i++){
        System.out.println("Input the number "+ (i+1));
        array[i] = sc.nextInt();    
    
    }

    //maximum
    int max= array[0];
    for(int i =0; i<n; i++){
        if(max < array[i]){
            max= array[i];
        }
    
   }
   System.out.println("Maximum of your numbers is "+ max);


   //minimum
    int min= array[0];
    for(int i =0; i<n; i++){
        if(min > array[i]){
            min= array[i];
        }
    
   }
   System.out.println("Minimum of your numbers is "+ min);
   //sum
